WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:03.230
- [Narrator] This bottle, this brand.

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.558
Unique and busy, yet simple and standard.

00:00:06.558 --> 00:00:07.616
You might've seen it.

00:00:07.616 --> 00:00:09.402
You might even use it.

00:00:09.402 --> 00:00:11.569
But have you ever read it?

00:00:14.171 --> 00:00:15.936
The Dr. Bronner
Brand is the top selling

00:00:15.936 --> 00:00:18.216
organic soap company in North America.

00:00:18.216 --> 00:00:20.515
And if you look closely at the label,

00:00:20.515 --> 00:00:23.695
you'll see quotes from Jesus,
Einstein, George Washington,

00:00:23.695 --> 00:00:27.896
you name it, you'll also read
a lot about the moral ABC.

00:00:27.896 --> 00:00:30.430
The brainchild of Dr. Emmanuel Bronner,

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.128
the founder of Dr. Bronner's Magic Soaps.

00:00:33.128 --> 00:00:34.825
Born into a Jewish family in Germany,

00:00:34.825 --> 00:00:37.211
he immigrated to Milwaukee in 1929

00:00:37.211 --> 00:00:39.756
and worked as a consultant
for various soap companies.

00:00:39.756 --> 00:00:42.283
But his real passion was philosophy.

00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:46.377
He had a vision for world peace,
and he called it moral ABC.

00:00:46.377 --> 00:00:47.459
Its mission read,

00:00:47.459 --> 00:00:49.434
- [Emmanuel] "In all we
do, let us be generous,

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:52.925
fair and loving to Spaceship
Earth and all its inhabitants.

00:00:52.925 --> 00:00:55.706
"For we're all-one or none, All-One."

00:00:55.706 --> 00:00:57.452
- [Narrator] Basically he
wanted people to set aside

00:00:57.452 --> 00:00:59.208
their religious and ethnic differences

00:00:59.208 --> 00:01:00.489
to find common ground.

00:01:00.489 --> 00:01:03.005
During WWII, Bronner began lecturing

00:01:03.005 --> 00:01:05.375
and spreading his vision
for peace and unity,

00:01:05.375 --> 00:01:07.295
and he started drawing crowds.

00:01:07.295 --> 00:01:08.686
(cheering)

00:01:08.686 --> 00:01:11.005
In 1947, during one of his lecture tours,

00:01:11.005 --> 00:01:13.165
Bronner was arrested for
giving a public speech

00:01:13.165 --> 00:01:16.684
without a permit, he wound
up in a mental institution.

00:01:16.684 --> 00:01:19.628
He escaped, and he made his
way to Southern California

00:01:19.628 --> 00:01:21.766
where he declared himself a doctor, rabbi,

00:01:21.766 --> 00:01:24.441
and alleged that he was Einstein's nephew.

00:01:24.441 --> 00:01:26.590
It was during this lecture
tour that Bronner began

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.440
giving his family's soap away.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.205
He quickly realized
people were only coming

00:01:30.205 --> 00:01:32.839
for the free soap, and
leaving before the lecture

00:01:32.839 --> 00:01:35.032
so Bronner started printing his scriptures

00:01:35.032 --> 00:01:36.806
and sticking them onto the bars.

00:01:36.806 --> 00:01:40.633
And just like that, Dr.
Bronner's Magic Soap was born.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.133
(jazzy music)

